Tracking architecture

The platform should distinguish between:

- A click recorded by Anchrr.
- An event received through an integration.
- A conversion confirmed by an external system.

Use understandable event statuses:

- Tracked.
- Click Recorded.
- Integration Required.
- Conversion Confirmed.

Tracking limitations

Do not claim that Anchrr can see what happens on an external website after redirecting a visitor unless that website provides tracking data through an installed pixel, API, webhook, postback, or supported integration.

Design the architecture so future integrations with ecommerce platforms such as Shopify and WooCommerce can be added.

Security

- API secrets must never be exposed in frontend code.
- Store secrets securely.
- Show secret values only when appropriate.
- Provide key creation and revocation controls.
- Validate incoming events.
- Protect tracking endpoints against abuse.

If a third-party integration requires credentials, show its connection status and setup instructions instead of inventing a working connection.

